            {
              "id": "GO-2024-2687",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[GO-2024-2687] HTTP/2 CONTINUATION flood in net/http"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "HTTP/2 CONTINUATION flood in net/http"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An attacker may cause an HTTP/2 endpoint to read arbitrary amounts of header data by sending an excessive number of CONTINUATION frames.\n\nMaintaining HPACK state requires parsing and processing all HEADERS and CONTINUATION frames on a connection. When a request's headers exceed MaxHeaderBytes, no memory is allocated to store the excess headers, but they are still parsed.\n\nThis permits an attacker to cause an HTTP/2 endpoint to read arbitrary amounts of header data, all associated with a request which is going to be rejected. These headers can include Huffman-encoded data which is significantly more expensive for the receiver to decode than for an attacker to send.\n\nThe fix sets a limit on the amount of excess header frames we will process before closing a connection."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2024-2687",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2023-45288",
                  "GHSA-4v7x-pqxf-cx7m"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2024-3333",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[GO-2024-3333] Non-linear parsing of case-insensitive content in golang.org/x/net/html"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Non-linear parsing of case-insensitive content in golang.org/x/net/html"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An attacker can craft an input to the Parse functions that would be processed non-linearly with respect to its length, resulting in extremely slow parsing. This could cause a denial of service."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2024-3333",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2024-45338",
                  "GHSA-w32m-9786-jp63"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2025-3503",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[GO-2025-3503] HTTP Proxy bypass using IPv6 Zone IDs in golang.org/x/net"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "HTTP Proxy bypass using IPv6 Zone IDs in golang.org/x/net"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Matching of hosts against proxy patterns can improperly treat an IPv6 zone ID as a hostname component. For example, when the NO_PROXY environment variable is set to \"*.example.com\", a request to \"[::1%25.example.com]:80` will incorrectly match and not be proxied."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2025-3503",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2025-22870",
                  "GHSA-qxp5-gwg8-xv66"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2025-3595",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[GO-2025-3595] Incorrect Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation in x/net in golang.org/x/net"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Incorrect Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation in x/net in golang.org/x/net"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The tokenizer incorrectly interprets tags with unquoted attribute values that end with a solidus character (/) as self-closing. When directly using Tokenizer, this can result in such tags incorrectly being marked as self-closing, and when using the Parse functions, this can result in content following such tags as being placed in the wrong scope during DOM construction, but only when tags are in foreign content (e.g. \u003cmath\u003e, \u003csvg\u003e, etc contexts)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2025-3595",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2025-22872"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-4440",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[GO-2026-4440] Quadratic parsing complexity in golang.org/x/net/html"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Quadratic parsing complexity in golang.org/x/net/html"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The html.Parse function in golang.org/x/net/html has quadratic parsing complexity when processing certain inputs, which can lead to denial of service (DoS) if an attacker provides specially crafted HTML content."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-4440",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2025-47911"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-4441",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[GO-2026-4441] Infinite parsing loop in golang.org/x/net"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Infinite parsing loop in golang.org/x/net"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The html.Parse function in golang.org/x/net/html has an infinite parsing loop when processing certain inputs, which can lead to denial of service (DoS) if an attacker provides specially crafted HTML content."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-4441",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2025-58190"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-4918",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[GO-2026-4918] Infinite loop in HTTP/2 transport when given bad SETTINGS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE in net/http/internal/http2 in golang.org/x/net"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Infinite loop in HTTP/2 transport when given bad SETTINGS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE in net/http/internal/http2 in golang.org/x/net"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "When processing HTTP/2 SETTINGS frames, transport will enter an infinite loop of writing CONTINUATION frames if it receives a SETTINGS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE with a value of 0."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-4918",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2026-33814"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-5025",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[GO-2026-5025] Invoking incorrect handling of namespaced elements in foreign content in golang.org/x/net/html"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Invoking incorrect handling of namespaced elements in foreign content in golang.org/x/net/html"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Parsing arbitrary HTML which is then rendered using Render can result in an unexpected HTML tree. This can be leveraged to execute XSS attacks in applications that attempt to sanitize input HTML before rendering."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-5025",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2026-42506"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-5026",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[GO-2026-5026] Invoking failure to reject ASCII-only Punycode-encoded labels in golang.org/x/net/idna"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Invoking failure to reject ASCII-only Punycode-encoded labels in golang.org/x/net/idna"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The ToASCII and ToUnicode functions incorrectly accept Punycode-encoded labels that decode to an ASCII-only label. For example, ToUnicode(\"xn--example-.com\") incorrectly returns the name \"example.com\" rather than an error.\n\nThis behavior can lead to privilege escalation in programs using the idna package. For example, a program which performs privilege checks on the ASCII hostname may reject \"example.com\" but permit \"xn--example-.com\". If that program subsequently converts the ASCII hostname to Unicode, it will inadvertently permits access to the Unicode name \"example.com\"."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-5026",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2026-39821"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-5027",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[GO-2026-5027] Invoking incorrect handling of HTML elements in foreign content in golang.org/x/net/html"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Invoking incorrect handling of HTML elements in foreign content in golang.org/x/net/html"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Parsing arbitrary HTML which is then rendered using Render can result in an unexpected HTML tree. This can be leveraged to execute XSS attacks in applications that attempt to sanitize input HTML before rendering."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-5027",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
